course: dictionary
lesson: 3905
title: Fright and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «The owl's sudden screech gave me a fright.» Ask: what would fit in the gap? A sudden scare fits, so here fright means a sudden feeling of fear.
explain: «I look a fright after the rain!» Here nobody is scared. The clue is "after the rain": the speaker means they look very untidy or strange. This is an old-fashioned meaning, so you will mostly meet it in older books and in sayings.
explain: «Almost everyone gets stage fright before a school play.» Stage fright is a fixed phrase, so read the whole phrase, not each word alone. It means the fear some people feel before performing in front of an audience.
fact: A fright is a sudden feeling of fear.
fact: Something that makes you suddenly afraid can also be called a fright.
fact: Stage fright is the fear some people feel before performing in front of an audience.
fact: «Take fright» means suddenly become scared, as a horse may take fright at a bag or a bird.
fact: Old use: «I look a fright» means someone looks very untidy or strange.
exercise: «The owl's sudden screech gave me a fright.» What does fright mean here? | A slow, quiet walk | A kind of owl | *A sudden feeling of fear | A bright light in the sky
exercise: Jess felt stage fright before the school play. What is stage fright? | A tired feeling after a long show | Being on a stage in the rain | A bright light used in theatres | *The fear some people feel before performing in front of an audience
exercise: «Riders wear helmets because a horse may take fright at a bag.» What does take fright mean? | *Suddenly become scared | Run away very slowly | Lie down and sleep | Fall over
test: «After the long run, Sam looked a fright.» What does a fright mean here? | A very brave person | A sudden feeling of fear | *Someone who looks very untidy or strange | A loud noise at night
test: «Jump scares should never be done near stairs, because a fright can make someone fall.» What does fright mean? | A kind of staircase | *A sudden feeling of fear | A hot drink | A joke that is funny for everyone
exam: Priya asks, "Is a fright always the same meaning?" What is the answer? | Yes, it always means a loud noise | Yes, it always means something funny | *No, the context shows whether it means fear, a scare, or an untidy look | No, it only ever means a horse
